@@ -130,6 +130,26 @@ The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each hold
 
 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+The veterinarian directory answers which specialties a veterinarian holds; staff also ask the inverse. The clinic therefore publishes a read-only specialty directory, reached at its own address. It lists every specialty the clinic knows by its stored name, each with the veterinarians holding it `[REQ-VET-003]`. Each veterinarian appears by full name, first name then last name. Every specialty appears on one page, never split across pages. The directory lists specialties, not the veterinarian roster, so a veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on it. No navigation entry or link from another page leads to it.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is listed by its stored name with the veterinarians holding it.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding a specialty, when the specialty directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown under it by first name, then last name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the specialty directory is opened, then that veterinarian does not appear.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given more specialties than one page of the veterinarian directory holds, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is on that one page.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A veterinarian holding several specialties appears under each of them.
+2. A specialty held by no veterinarian is still listed, with no veterinarian under it.
+3. Specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+4. A specialty's name is shown as stored, not translated into the reader's language.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
